course: dictionary
lesson: 10086
title: Many jobs of one small word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «There» is a small word with several jobs, and the words around it tell you which job it has. Sometimes it says that something exists: «There are always far fewer predators than plant-eaters.» Here it means that these animals are in the world, not that they are in a particular place.
explain: Sometimes «there» means in that place, or to that place, not here: «The actors are really there, right in front of you.» Notice the clue: the words «in front of you» show that «there» is about a place near the actors, away from the reader. Ask yourself: could I swap it for «in that place»? If so, that is its meaning.
explain: «There» can also point or comfort. «There goes the bus!» points at the bus. «There, there» is said softly to calm someone who is upset, like a hug in words. The feeling in the sentence tells you which one it is.
explain: In casual talk, people say «there's 3 left» and «there ya go». «There ya go» means here it is, or well done. In a formal exam, you may see «there remain» or «there exists», which mean the same as «there are» or «there is». The clues in the sentence will always help you.
fact: «There» can mean that something exists: «there are 3 birds».
fact: «There» can mean in that place or to that place, as in «over there» or «get there».
fact: «There» can point at something, as in «There goes the bus!».
fact: «There, there» is said to calm someone who is upset.
fact: «There you go» means here it is, or well done.
exercise: «There are 3 birds in the tree.» What does there mean in this sentence? | *It says that 3 birds exist or are in the tree | It asks a question about the birds | It is used to calm a bird down | It means to that place, far away
exercise: «There goes the bus!» What is there doing in this sentence? | Calming the bus down | Saying the bus is broken | *Pointing at the bus | Asking where the bus has gone
exercise: «To find how many there were at the start, begin at the end.» What does there mean here? | A question about the end | A place far away from here | A word said to calm someone | *The things that existed at the start
test: Mum says «There, there» to Sam, who has just fallen over. What is she doing? | Pointing at Sam | Asking Sam how many times he has fallen | *Calming Sam because he is upset | Telling Sam he is far away
test: In «there and back», what does there mean? | *To a place away from here, and then home again | A ticket for the bus | In this exact spot, right now | In the wrong place
exam: In the formal exam voice, «there remain 5 sweets» means the same as which phrase? | There were 5 sweets yesterday | *There are still 5 sweets left | Five sweets, please | The sweets are over there and far away
